// Why Ghana, and why now section
---
<!-- =====================================================================
     WHY GHANA, AND WHY NOW — the case, for anyone still weighing it up.
     Kept behind the form rather than in front of it.
     ===================================================================== -->
<section id="why-ghana" class="shell band scroll-mt-20 border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-[clamp(26px,3.2vw,46px)]">

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 max-w-[46ch]">
      <p class="kicker reveal">Why Ghana, and why now</p>
      <h2 class="display d-md reveal" style="--d:80ms">
        Four reasons, not one.
      </h2>
      <!-- The write-up's opening line only. The two sentences that followed it
           repeated the landing page almost word for word, and at this point on
           the page the reader has already had that argument. -->
      <p class="copy reveal max-w-none" style="--d:120ms">
        Ghana has decided to become Africa&rsquo;s AI hub &mdash; and is putting
        real money, policy and talent behind the ambition.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Two up, on the page grid, rather than one narrow column with the rules
         running out into empty space beside it. -->
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-[clamp(28px,4vw,64px)] gap-y-[clamp(18px,2.2vw,30px)]">
      <div class="flex gap-5 border-t border-hairline pt-[clamp(16px,1.8vw,22px)] reveal" style="--d:80ms">
        <span class="kicker shrink-0 pt-[3px] w-[24px]">01</span>
        <p class="text-[14px] leading-[1.7] text-body">
          <strong class="text-ink">A national commitment, not a pilot.</strong>
          In April 2026 Ghana launched a ten-year National AI Strategy backed by roughly USD&nbsp;270 million &mdash; including USD&nbsp;250 million for a national AI computing centre intended to serve research, enterprise and the wider region.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-5 border-t border-hairline pt-[clamp(16px,1.8vw,22px)] reveal" style="--d:150ms">
        <span class="kicker shrink-0 pt-[3px] w-[24px]">02</span>
        <p class="text-[14px] leading-[1.7] text-body">
          <strong class="text-ink">Talent, at scale.</strong>
          A young, English-speaking graduate population, and a digital services sector that already employs more than 20,000 people. Ghana&rsquo;s ambition is to add 100,000 more.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-5 border-t border-hairline pt-[clamp(16px,1.8vw,22px)] reveal" style="--d:220ms">
        <span class="kicker shrink-0 pt-[3px] w-[24px]">03</span>
        <p class="text-[14px] leading-[1.7] text-body">
          <strong class="text-ink">A shortage worth solving.</strong>
          Germany and the DACH region have carried well over 100,000 unfilled ICT positions in recent years. Accra sits an hour or two from Frankfurt &mdash; the same working day, not the other side of the world.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-5 border-t border-hairline pt-[clamp(16px,1.8vw,22px)] reveal" style="--d:290ms">
        <span class="kicker shrink-0 pt-[3px] w-[24px]">04</span>
        <p class="text-[14px] leading-[1.7] text-body">
          <strong class="text-ink">German partnership already on the ground.</strong>
          Through FAIR Forward &ndash; Artificial Intelligence for All and the Invest for Jobs Special Initiative, German Development Cooperation has spent years in Ghana building AI skills, open data and policy foundations on behalf of the Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
